From: RK3128 reference <reference@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: guard RK3128 runtime power-down with PMU idle

Apply after the764 shared RNG-owner patch. Drain IRQ and START before
requesting crypto NoC idle, then reset and gate at unchanged clock rates.
Resume the port before MMIO. Keep runtime PM diagnostic-only after the
failed reboot handoff. Serialize RNG and crypto PM references,
retain continuous health history and pin all uncertain failure states.
Only the guarded hash-DMA and cipher-PIO profile may use runtime PM.

Signed-off-by: RK3128 reference <reference@example.invalid>

diff --git a/drivers/crypto/Kconfig b/drivers/crypto/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/crypto/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/crypto/Kconfig
@@ -709,6 +709,17 @@
 	  primitive at priority 1, below CPU implementations. Diagnostic
 	  parameters cannot enable cipher DMA in this configuration.
 
+config CRYPTO_DEV_RK3128_RUNTIME_PM
+	bool "Diagnostic RK3128 crypto PMU idle runtime power management"
+	depends on CRYPTO_DEV_RK3128_HASH_PIO && CRYPTO_SELFTESTS_FULL && PM
+	default n
+	help
+	  Use bounded crypto NoC idle acknowledgment before reset and clock
+	  gating. Only the guarded hash-DMA, cipher-PIO and hwrng profile may
+	  use this sequence. Failures retain power and the binding until reboot.
+	  Reboot from a suspended port failed; do not enable in normal images.
+	  This option is for guarded full-test investigations only.
+
 config CRYPTO_DEV_ROCKCHIP_DEBUG
 	bool "Enable Rockchip crypto stats"
 	depends on CRYPTO_DEV_ROCKCHIP
